      "url": "https://github.com/huggingface/blog/blob/main/multi-vector-encoder.md",
      "snippet": "Where a regular embedding model compresses a whole text into one vector, a multi-vector model keeps one vector per token and scores query against document with the MaxSim operator. That preserves token-level matching information that a single vector has to average away, which usually means stronger retrieval at the cost of a bigger index. It&#x27;s also the state of the art for visual document ..."
